1
00:00:02,440 --> 00:00:04,840
虚无
Nothingness.

2
00:00:04,950 --> 00:00:07,600
万物之始也
It is the beginning

3
00:00:07,720 --> 00:00:11,500
而万物皆归于无。
and the end of all creation.

4
00:00:11,620 --> 00:00:13,620
然则何谓无乎？
But what is it?

5
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:17,050
空者果真为空？
Is empty space really empty?

6
00:00:18,260 --> 00:00:20,660
抑或其实为暗能量所充斥...
Or is it filled with hidden forces...

7
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:24,430
...它是使宇宙从大爆炸中诞生的第一推动...
...forces that exploded our Universe into existence...

8
00:00:25,860 --> 00:00:29,720
...还是终结我们所知一切的末日审判？
...or forces that could destroy reality as we know it?

9
00:00:29,840 --> 00:00:32,470
无究竟为何物？
What is nothing?

10
00:00:36,840 --> 00:00:41,480
《同摩根·弗里曼一起穿越虫洞》
空间、时间、生命本身
Space, time, life itself.

11
00:00:43,750 --> 00:00:48,590
宇宙的秘密，尽在穿越虫洞
The secrets of the cosmos lie through the wormhole.

12
00:00:53,750 --> 00:00:58,590
无究竟为何物？

13
00:01:01,910 --> 00:01:04,800
无者
The void.

14
00:01:04,910 --> 00:01:07,570
依《圣经》所云，
The Bible says it was the place

15
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:12,010
“无”乃神创天地之所在也。
from which God brought forth the heavens and the earth.

16
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:16,510
现在的科学家对此有自己的理解
Scientists now have their own version of that belief.

17
00:01:16,630 --> 00:01:19,650
他们称其为“大爆炸”
They call it the Big Bang.

18
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:24,720
但是有又何以生于无呢？
But how can something come from what appears to be nothing?

19
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:27,960
理解虚无的本质
Understanding the true nature of nothingness

20
00:01:28,070 --> 00:01:30,760
或许是现代科学最深奥，最令人费解
is perhaps the deepest and most-baffling conundrum

21
00:01:30,870 --> 00:01:32,890
…的难题。
in modern science.

22
00:01:33,010 --> 00:01:35,660
它能解释宇宙从何而来
It could explain where the Universe came from

23
00:01:35,780 --> 00:01:38,030
也能说明我们所知所爱的一切
and whether everything we know and love

24
00:01:38,150 --> 00:01:41,950
能否再次从零开始。
could turn into nothing once again.

25
00:01:47,150 --> 00:01:51,710
“混沌初开之时，世界空无一物”
"In the beginning, the earth was without form."

26
00:01:51,830 --> 00:01:53,680
你正当年少时，
When you were young,

27
00:01:53,790 --> 00:01:55,650
可曾闭目而思
did you ever close your eyes

28
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:58,650
神游于无垠之玄境，
and try to imagine floating in total darkness,

29
00:01:58,770 --> 00:02:01,790
去体验真正的虚无？
to experience absolute nothing?

30
00:02:01,900 --> 00:02:03,420
我干过
I did.

31
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:06,260
而且我总是失败。
And I always failed.

32
00:02:06,370 --> 00:02:07,630
无论如何，
No matter what,

33
00:02:07,740 --> 00:02:11,930
我都不能清空我心脏不停的脉动
I could not rid this void of the pulse of my heartbeat

34
00:02:12,050 --> 00:02:14,100
和思想中无尽的杂念
and the thoughts in my head.

35
00:02:14,210 --> 00:02:15,870
当我想象时，
When I imagine,

36
00:02:15,980 --> 00:02:19,210
我不能阻止去想象一些 东西
I can't help but imagine something,

37
00:02:19,320 --> 00:02:21,720
而不是四大皆空
not nothing.

38
00:02:30,460 --> 00:02:32,690
Slava Turyshev是美国航天局的物理学家
Slava Turyshev is a NASA physicist

39
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:35,990
他一直梦想着空无
who has always dreamed of nothing

40
00:02:36,100 --> 00:02:39,810
以及怎么遇见真空
and what nothing might be like to visit.

41
00:02:44,310 --> 00:02:46,700
我出生的那个镇
The town I was born in

42
00:02:46,810 --> 00:02:51,670
正好坐落于从拜科努尔发射来的火箭的弹道之下
was just under the trajectory rockets launched from Baikonur.

43
00:02:51,790 --> 00:02:53,840
那是一个俄罗斯的发射场。
It's a Russian launch site.

44
00:02:53,950 --> 00:02:58,080
所以正是这些构成了我的主要印象
So that actually made a major impression on me.

45
00:02:58,190 --> 00:03:01,950
Slava整个童年都做火箭
Slava spent his childhood building rockets

46
00:03:02,060 --> 00:03:04,520
他希望有朝一日能乘坐其中一枚
and yearned to one day ride one

47
00:03:04,630 --> 00:03:06,700
飞向那空荡荡的外太空
into the emptiness of outer space.

48
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:20,970
但命运有其他安排。
But fate had other plans.

49
00:03:21,080 --> 00:03:24,070
我想成为一名太空飞行者，
I wanted to be on a space flight,

50
00:03:24,180 --> 00:03:27,310
而且也确实训练过一段时间
and at one of those times actually was training

51
00:03:27,420 --> 00:03:30,580
结果上世纪90年代末俄罗斯飞船都被召回，
for the Russian space shuttle back in late '90s,

52
00:03:30,690 --> 00:03:33,250
然后所有项目就都取消了。
just before the program was canceled.

53
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:35,480
没有老毛子飞船，
With no Russian shuttle,

54
00:03:35,600 --> 00:03:38,490
Slava失去了上太空的机会，
Slava lost his ticket to outer space,

55
00:03:38,600 --> 00:03:40,390
但是作为一名物理学家，
but as a physicist,

56
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:43,960
他发现与充满天际的那些一样类型的空间
he discovered that the same space that fills the heavens

57
00:03:44,070 --> 00:03:46,960
同样存在于地球上。
also exists everywhere on earth.

58
00:03:47,070 --> 00:03:49,830
只不过地上的这里没那么空荡荡
It's just not empty down here.

59
00:03:49,940 --> 00:03:52,700
而且,探索空间的基本性质
And exploring the fundamental properties of space

60
00:03:52,810 --> 00:03:55,170
并不需要一个数十亿美元的火箭。
does not require a billion-dollar rocket.

61
00:03:55,280 --> 00:03:58,520
事实上,你所需要的也就是一桶水而已。
In fact, all you need is a bucket of water.

62
00:04:01,090 --> 00:04:03,540
这绝对是个超简单的实验。
This is actually a very simple experiment.

63
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:06,510
我要做的就是把水倒进桶里转一转
What I'll do, I'll put some water in the bucket,

64
00:04:06,630 --> 00:04:11,030
其实这个鬼点子是牛顿那家伙出的
and this experiment actually was thought by Isaac Newton.

65
00:04:15,370 --> 00:04:16,760
目的，当然是，
The objective, of course,

66
00:04:16,870 --> 00:04:19,770
看看当我们旋转桶时水会发生什么现象
to see what's going on with the water when we spin the bucket.

67
00:04:23,740 --> 00:04:28,350
好了，我们转转它好，非常好
So, let's spin it very, very nice.

68
00:04:30,380 --> 00:04:32,210
好的，稳定住
So, stable.

69
00:04:32,320 --> 00:04:36,010
你可以观察到桶中的水持平。
You can observe that the water in the bucket is staying flat.

70
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:38,290
让我们看看会发生什么。
And let's see what happens.

71
00:04:39,490 --> 00:04:41,950
艾萨克·牛顿认为水的步调
Isaac Newton thought that the water

72
00:04:42,060 --> 00:04:44,420
应该与桶旋转的步调一致
ought to spin in lockstep with the bucket,

73
00:04:44,530 --> 00:04:46,790
就好比我们随地球一起旋转
just as we move with the spinning earth.

74
00:04:46,900 --> 00:04:48,520
但是水根本就不动
But the water does not move

75
00:04:48,640 --> 00:04:50,830
至少在开始转桶时是这样
with the spinning bucket at first.

76
00:04:50,940 --> 00:04:53,960
最终，桶内壁的摩擦力
Eventually, friction from the inner wall of the bucket

77
00:04:54,070 --> 00:04:56,340
拖曳着水向上运动
drags the water upwards.

78
00:04:58,040 --> 00:04:59,830
所以，你看
So, you can see

79
00:04:59,950 --> 00:05:03,800
水在桶中慢慢向上
that the water is slowly going upwards in the bucket.

80
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:07,210
但是在桶开始运动的那一刻
But in the first moments after the bucket is set in motion,

81
00:05:07,320 --> 00:05:10,280
水还是没动
the water stays still.

82
00:05:10,390 --> 00:05:14,580
牛顿意识到一定有什么东西阻滞了水的运动
Newton realized there must be something gluing the water

83
00:05:14,700 --> 00:05:17,220
使其分离于周边的庞大世界
to the larger world around it.

84
00:05:17,330 --> 00:05:21,460
他认为这种胶水就是空间本身
He thought that glue must be space itself,

85
00:05:21,570 --> 00:05:25,560
它在桶内桶外无处不在。
which exists all around and inside the bucket.

86
00:05:25,670 --> 00:05:28,860
事实上，我们不能想当然地认为空间是什么都没有。
Indeed, we cannot assume that space is nothing.

87
00:05:28,980 --> 00:05:30,100
它其实是一种物质
There is something,

88
00:05:30,210 --> 00:05:33,730
正是这种物质影响了物体的运动
and that something influences how matter moves.

89
00:05:33,850 --> 00:05:35,640
牛顿并没有解释
Newton could not explain

90
00:05:35,750 --> 00:05:39,310
原本空无一物的空间是如何发挥物质作用的
how the nothingness of space was somehow something.

91
00:05:39,420 --> 00:05:42,410
然而，在1915年，爱因斯坦的
But in 1915, Albert Einstein's

92
00:05:42,520 --> 00:05:45,680
革命性理论——广义相对论
revolutionary Theory of General Relativity

93
00:05:45,790 --> 00:05:49,480
表明牛顿的思想基本正确
showed that Newton's idea was fundamentally right.

94
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:54,920
空间，或者按他的新定义，时空
Space or, as he reformulated it, Space-Time

95
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:56,760
是如可弯曲的织物一般
is a bendable fabric

96
00:05:56,870 --> 00:06:00,940
将宇宙中万事万物编织在一起
into of which all the matter in the Universe is woven.

97
00:06:08,580 --> 00:06:11,510
空间填充于我们宇宙的每一个角落
The space that fills every corner of our Universe

98
00:06:11,620 --> 00:06:15,380
所有事物都在其中进行着永恒的拔河比赛
plays a constant game of tug of war with all the things in it,

99
00:06:15,490 --> 00:06:20,350
无论是行星，一桶水抑或一叠纸概莫能外
be they planets, water in a bucket, or a stack of papers.

100
00:06:20,460 --> 00:06:22,950
所以空无一物的空间也不是无
So if empty space is not nothing,

101
00:06:23,060 --> 00:06:25,720
那什么是无呢？
then what is it?

102
00:06:25,830 --> 00:06:28,490
Frank Close是一名量子物理学家
Frank Close is a particle physicist.

103
00:06:28,600 --> 00:06:32,060
他研究认为真空的能量
He's learned that the power of empty space

104
00:06:32,170 --> 00:06:34,360
绝不可被低估
should never be underestimated.

105
00:06:34,470 --> 00:06:37,000
-嗨, Andrew. -嗨, Frank.
-Hi, Andrew. -Hi, Frank.

106
00:06:37,110 --> 00:06:39,970
那么,它是一个铁桶,
So, it's a metal drum,

107
00:06:40,080 --> 00:06:43,370
而你什么都不做就能令其崩塌
and you can make it collapse by doing nothing.

108
00:06:43,480 --> 00:06:44,870
这是气泵
That's rig.

109
00:06:44,990 --> 00:06:46,370
我们将利用真空之力
We're gonna use the power of nothing.

110
00:06:46,490 --> 00:06:49,880
所以，这是非常戏剧性的。我更好的做到了,对吗？
So, this is pretty dramatic. I better put this on, right?

111
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:51,670
我想我们是,欧耶。
Guess we had, yeah.

112
00:06:51,780 --> 00:06:52,860
还有什么我该怎么办？
And what else do I do?

113
00:06:52,980 --> 00:06:55,090
那么，如果你只是帮我切换泵的话
So, if you just switch on the pump for me.

114
00:07:11,220 --> 00:07:12,290
真空之力
The power of nothing.

115
00:07:12,400 --> 00:07:16,120
我们把桶内的空气全部抽走
We took all of the air out of the inside of this drum.

116
00:07:16,240 --> 00:07:18,190
外面的大气制造了
The atmosphere on the outside

117
00:07:18,310 --> 00:07:21,460
约每平方米十吨的力
was making a 10-tons-every-square-meter force

118
00:07:21,580 --> 00:07:25,330
在桶上--这抵抗对于金属来说太强烈了
on that drum -- far too strong for the metal to resist.

119
00:07:25,450 --> 00:07:26,970
崩毁
Collapse.

120
00:07:27,080 --> 00:07:28,770
那么，里面什么都没有
So, nothing on the inside.

121
00:07:28,880 --> 00:07:30,370
外面有10到20吨的压力
10 or 20 tons on the outside.

122
00:07:30,480 --> 00:07:31,480
嘣!
Bingo!

123
00:07:32,850 --> 00:07:36,880
在他为理解自然基本力的探索中,
In his quest to understand the fundamental forces of nature,

124
00:07:36,990 --> 00:07:39,750
Frank发现空无的空间还能比
Frank has discovered that empty space can do far more

125
00:07:39,860 --> 00:07:42,880
制造固体爆裂做更多的事
than cause solid matter to implode.

126
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:46,650
他认为真空干扰了所有物质的行为
He thinks it is interfering with everything matter does.

127
00:07:46,770 --> 00:07:48,190
在19世纪，
In the 19th century,

128
00:07:48,300 --> 00:07:50,530
人们认为如果你抽走所有空气，
they thought if you take all the air out,

129
00:07:50,640 --> 00:07:53,290
你留下的是一个真正的空真空。
what you're left with is a genuinely empty vacuum.

130
00:07:53,410 --> 00:07:55,430
这观念根深蒂固
And that is how it could have stayed

131
00:07:55,540 --> 00:07:58,570
直到我们发现了量子理论思想
except that we then discovered the idea of Quantum Theory.

132
00:07:58,680 --> 00:08:02,470
量子理论的伟大奥秘之一
And one of the great mysteries underlying Quantum Theory

133
00:08:02,580 --> 00:08:04,940
旨在极短的时间内，
is that at an instant in time,

134
00:08:05,050 --> 00:08:08,210
你不能确切的知道能量的多寡
you cannot be absolutely sure how much energy there is.

135
00:08:08,320 --> 00:08:11,280
能量可以被借用，还能在
Energy can be borrowed or exchanged around

136
00:08:11,390 --> 00:08:13,310
极短时间尺度内到处交流
on very short time scales.

137
00:08:13,430 --> 00:08:15,320
所以，在现代量子理论中，
So, in modern Quantum Theory,

138
00:08:15,430 --> 00:08:18,120
真空是一个很暴力的场所
the vacuum is a very violent place,

139
00:08:18,230 --> 00:08:19,390
即便是你与我，
even though you and I,

140
00:08:19,500 --> 00:08:21,620
日复一日观察，不能察觉一点端倪
day-to-day, aren't aware of that fact.

141
00:08:21,740 --> 00:08:25,690
空的空间中能量不断冒泡
Empty space is a froth of bubbling energy,

142
00:08:25,810 --> 00:08:28,030
像熔融金属一样。
like molten metal.

143
00:08:28,140 --> 00:08:30,130
Frank和他的量子物理学同事
And Frank and his fellow particle physicists

144
00:08:30,240 --> 00:08:32,930
现已证明这种能量
now have proof that this energy

145
00:08:33,050 --> 00:08:35,540
阻挡我们观测宇宙基本力
shields us from seeing the true strength

146
00:08:35,650 --> 00:08:38,340
的真实实力——
of the fundamental forces of the Universe --

147
00:08:38,450 --> 00:08:41,040
比如带电粒子间
forces like the electrical repulsion

148
00:08:41,160 --> 00:08:42,840
的电斥力。
between charged particles.

149
00:08:42,960 --> 00:08:45,380
那么，我们假定电子在这，
So, we imagine an electron sitting here,

150
00:08:45,490 --> 00:08:48,620
它的电场穿过空间四面传播
spreading out its electrical tentacles through space,

151
00:08:48,730 --> 00:08:51,150
我将用另一个电子放这儿
and I got another electron here that I will use

152
00:08:51,270 --> 00:08:53,720
然后我将测量它们之间的力，
and I'll measure the force between them,

153
00:08:53,830 --> 00:08:55,190
它们离得越近，
and the closer it gets,

154
00:08:55,300 --> 00:08:57,430
力也会越来越大。
the force will rise more and more.

155
00:08:57,540 --> 00:09:00,860
但是我们现在知道，由于量子效应，
But we now know, because of the Quantum Theory,

156
00:09:00,980 --> 00:09:02,930
那个小电子在那里
is that that little electron sitting there

157
00:09:03,040 --> 00:09:05,170
它不是一个孤立状态。
is actually not isolated.

158
00:09:05,280 --> 00:09:09,200
它被量子真空环绕着。
It is surrounded by the quantum vacuum.

159
00:09:09,320 --> 00:09:12,670
所以，它是一个被笼罩的电子
So, it's an electron in a shroud.

160
00:09:12,790 --> 00:09:17,210
罩的这一团雾会对电场力产生强烈影响
And that shroud reduces the full impact of its electrical force.

161
00:09:17,330 --> 00:09:19,510
同样的效应也会出现在另一个电子身上
The same thing is true of this other electron.

162
00:09:19,630 --> 00:09:21,680
Frank认为
Frank believes

163
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:24,720
我们对于电磁力的任何历史测量
that all historical measurements of the electrical force

164
00:09:24,830 --> 00:09:28,720
因为这种能量覆盖的缘故都是不准确的
are inaccurate because of these energy shrouds.

165
00:09:28,840 --> 00:09:30,890
但是现在的粒子加速器，
But now atom smashers,

166
00:09:31,010 --> 00:09:33,900
比如在瑞士日内瓦的大型强子对撞机
like the Large Hadron Collider in Geneva, Switzerland,

167
00:09:34,010 --> 00:09:36,160
能告诉我们完整的故事
can tell the full story.

168
00:09:36,280 --> 00:09:38,730
这里，亚原子粒子们
Here, subatomic particles collide

169
00:09:38,850 --> 00:09:42,900
以超过每小时6.7亿英里的速度碰撞
at more than 670 million miles per hour.

170
00:09:43,020 --> 00:09:45,640
它们彼此距离如此之近
They get so close to one another

171
00:09:45,750 --> 00:09:49,050
以至于它们最终捅破了那层覆盖
that they finally pierce the shroud.

172
00:09:51,660 --> 00:09:54,650
终于两者的覆盖云彼此交织，
But eventually the clouds get inside each other,

173
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:57,090
这也是事情变得有意思的时候，
and that's when it gets interesting,

174
00:09:57,200 --> 00:09:59,950
两团云雾开始向周围发散，
and the clouds then are so disbursed around,

175
00:10:00,070 --> 00:10:02,560
最终我们看到一个裸电子
we at last see the bare electron

176
00:10:02,670 --> 00:10:04,430
向另一个裸电子施加效应
acting on the other bare electron.

177
00:10:04,540 --> 00:10:06,660
此时也正是我们发现其中的作用力
And that's when we discover that the force

178
00:10:06,770 --> 00:10:09,240
远远超乎之前预测的时候
is much more dramatic than we'd thought before.

179
00:10:10,680 --> 00:10:12,700
就像防护眼镜
Just like protective eyewear

180
00:10:12,810 --> 00:10:15,600
阻挡危险的光线直射一样,
that shields a welder from dangerously intense light,

181
00:10:15,720 --> 00:10:19,010
Frank认为真空本身
Frank believes that empty space itself

182
00:10:19,120 --> 00:10:20,440
将宇宙
is insulating the Universe

183
00:10:20,550 --> 00:10:25,280
从真实的自然力强度中绝缘出来。
from the true intensity of the forces of nature.

184
00:10:25,390 --> 00:10:29,050
如果有可能把电子从那层披风中剥离出来,
If it was possible to turn off that cloak around the electron,

185
00:10:29,160 --> 00:10:32,420
你必须关闭真空的所有效应,
you'd have turned off all of the effects of the vacuum,

186
00:10:32,530 --> 00:10:34,760
事实上，你必须与此同时，
and you would actually, at the same time,

187
00:10:34,870 --> 00:10:36,460
摧毁了整个宇宙
have destroyed the Universe.

188
00:10:36,570 --> 00:10:37,960
因为所有的物质--
Because all structure --

189
00:10:38,070 --> 00:10:40,430
所有原子和分子的存在 --
the existence of atoms and molecules --

190
00:10:40,540 --> 00:10:43,670
都因量子效应而使得覆盖云出现
could not be if it wasn't for the Quantum Theory.

191
00:10:43,780 --> 00:10:48,500
如果没有这层能量覆盖在真空中四处躁动,
Without the dampening energy buzzing around in the vacuum,

192
00:10:48,620 --> 00:10:52,540
自然基本力将会全面失控。
the fundamental forces of nature would run out of control.

193
00:10:52,650 --> 00:10:56,180
我们的整个宇宙都会分崩离析
Our entire Universe would break apart.

194
00:10:56,290 --> 00:10:59,710
但这还只是其中的一方面
But that is only one side of the story.

195
00:10:59,830 --> 00:11:03,850
正因这层阻尼导流罩被从里面锁上了
Because locked inside this dampening shroud,

196
00:11:03,960 --> 00:11:06,420
那里应该有足够的能量去引发一场大爆炸
there should be enough energy to trigger an explosion

197
00:11:06,530 --> 00:11:10,360
其杀伤力会超过我们所知的任何爆炸
deadlier than anything we have ever known.

198
00:11:10,470 --> 00:11:16,180
真空似乎成了一个蓄势待发的火药桶
Empty space might be a powder keg waiting to explode.

199
00:11:20,280 --> 00:11:23,600
知道这些或许会令你吃惊
It might surprise you to know that our best theory

200
00:11:23,720 --> 00:11:27,470
我们有关宇宙在微观层面运行的最好理论
of how the Universe works down at the microscopic level --

201
00:11:27,660 --> 00:11:29,580
量子力学理论
the Theory of Quantum Mechanics

202
00:11:29,700 --> 00:11:34,290
也预测真空中蕴含着足够多的能量
also predicts empty space has enough energy

203
00:11:34,400 --> 00:11:37,770
把整个宇宙煮个稀巴烂
to boil the Universe out of existence.

204
00:11:39,410 --> 00:11:41,830
但这并没有发生
But it doesn't.

205
00:11:41,940 --> 00:11:45,930
一定有什么保证了我们相安无事
Something must be keeping nothing in check.

206
00:11:46,050 --> 00:11:47,900
问题是...
Question is...

207
00:11:48,020 --> 00:11:49,720
它是什么？
what?

208
00:11:54,190 --> 00:11:57,680
Neal Weiner是一名纽约大学的
Neal Weiner is a theoretical physicist

209
00:11:57,790 --> 00:11:59,810
理论物理学家
at New York University.

210
00:11:59,930 --> 00:12:02,720
他研究诸如日内瓦的大型强子对撞机
He studies the showers of subatomic particles

211
00:12:02,830 --> 00:12:06,090
或者芝加哥的兆电子伏特加速器所制造的
produced by atom smashers like the LHC in Geneva

212
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:09,690
亚原子粒子阵雨
and the Tevatron in Chicago.

213
00:12:09,800 --> 00:12:12,790
那么,假定有两个石头
So, suppose that you take these two rocks

214
00:12:12,910 --> 00:12:14,560
你把它们想象成质子
and you think of them as protons.

215
00:12:14,680 --> 00:12:17,100
你在相反方向使其碰撞,
You collide them together from opposite directions,

216
00:12:17,210 --> 00:12:18,300
当你这么做时,
and when you do that,

217
00:12:18,410 --> 00:12:20,170
在碰撞中将有足够能量
you have enough energy in the collision

218
00:12:20,280 --> 00:12:21,940
去制造粒子
that you can actually make particles

219
00:12:22,050 --> 00:12:23,270
有些粒子闻所未闻
that you would never think of

220
00:12:23,380 --> 00:12:25,210
比如单个质子碎片之类的
as being part of the individual protons.

221
00:12:25,320 --> 00:12:28,180
我的工作就是试图在当他们把两个粒子
My job is to try to make sense of what they find

222
00:12:28,290 --> 00:12:31,180
碰撞在一起时理解他们的发现
when they've collided these particles together.

223
00:12:31,290 --> 00:12:33,980
但为了理解这些
But to understand the shrapnel

224
00:12:34,100 --> 00:12:36,990
飞散的亚原子粒子
flying out of these subatomic explosions,

225
00:12:37,100 --> 00:12:41,420
Neal 必须以一种貌似古怪的方式审视宇宙
Neal must look at the Universe in a way that seems strange.

226
00:12:41,540 --> 00:12:44,690
他必须将构成固体物质的最小单位
He must see the smallest building blocks of solid matter

227
00:12:44,810 --> 00:12:47,900
视作非固体
as not solid at all.

228
00:12:48,010 --> 00:12:51,100
在量子领域，如果你创造了粒子,
In the Quantum realm, if you create particles,

229
00:12:51,210 --> 00:12:54,170
你创造时它们的情形更像是波
you're creating them in a state that looks more like a wave

230
00:12:54,280 --> 00:12:55,740
而不像是粒子
than it does like a particle.

231
00:12:55,850 --> 00:12:57,710
就好比喷泉,
Just like we have in a fountain,

232
00:12:57,820 --> 00:12:59,310
水流不断落下
where you have water coming down

233
00:12:59,420 --> 00:13:02,280
波动亦随之自中心而向四周扩散,
and sourcing waves that then spread out from a central point,

234
00:13:02,390 --> 00:13:04,210
在量子力学中，当你追溯粒子的来源,
in Quantum Mechanics, when you source a particle,

235
00:13:04,330 --> 00:13:06,280
你得到的是自中心点扩散的波，
you have a wave that spreads out from a central point,

236
00:13:06,390 --> 00:13:07,680
而不是在任何指定方向上
rather than a particular particle

237
00:13:07,800 --> 00:13:09,830
的特定粒子
going in any given direction.

238
00:13:11,400 --> 00:13:14,490
就像池塘水面上的涟漪,
Just like the ripples on the surface of a pond,

239
00:13:14,600 --> 00:13:16,320
粒子波将在整个空间海洋中
a particle wave will spread itself

240
00:13:16,440 --> 00:13:18,890
传播其自身,
over the entire ocean of space,

241
00:13:19,010 --> 00:13:23,160
那意味着在宇宙中任意一点,
and that means that at every point in the Universe,

242
00:13:23,280 --> 00:13:25,270
都存在
there exists ripples

243
00:13:25,380 --> 00:13:28,870
千万亿亿亿记的粒子波在扩散
from trillions upon trillions of particle waves.

244
00:13:28,980 --> 00:13:33,140
世上不存在绝对真空
There is no such thing as empty space.

245
00:13:33,250 --> 00:13:37,110
而能量就储存在这振荡不息的海洋中
And the energy contained in that great rippling ocean

246
00:13:37,230 --> 00:13:40,820
并导致了宇宙的膨胀
is causing the Universe to expand.

247
00:13:40,930 --> 00:13:43,420
当你观察宇宙膨胀时,
When you look at the expansion of the Universe,

248
00:13:43,530 --> 00:13:46,420
你会发现星系,星系团，所有的一切都膨胀开来 --
you see galaxies, galaxy clusters, all expanding away --

249
00:13:46,530 --> 00:13:48,620
所有一切都彼此相离而去
everything flying away from each other.

250
00:13:48,740 --> 00:13:52,330
结果发现宇宙并没有停下来的意思
And it turns out that the Universe is not slowing down.

251
00:13:52,440 --> 00:13:54,560
事实上宇宙在加速膨胀
The Universe is actually speeding up its expansion.

252
00:13:54,680 --> 00:13:55,830
宇宙在加速
The Universe is accelerating.

253
00:13:55,940 --> 00:13:58,400
所以我们对此唯一的解释是
So the only way that we know how to explain this

254
00:13:58,510 --> 00:14:01,470
假定一种类似于能量的东西
is if there's something like an energy density

255
00:14:01,580 --> 00:14:05,170
它的密度充斥整个空间
that is pervasive in Space itself.

256
00:14:05,290 --> 00:14:06,540
如果它确实存在,
If you have that,

257
00:14:06,650 --> 00:14:10,280
势必导致宇宙的加速膨胀
that's going to cause the Universe to accelerate.

258
00:14:10,390 --> 00:14:13,520
物理学家称其为“暗能量”
Physicists call this "dark energy."

259
00:14:13,630 --> 00:14:16,720
通过宇宙的膨胀速率,
From the rate of expansion of the Universe,

260
00:14:16,830 --> 00:14:20,520
人们能测算出真空中含多少暗能量
they can measure how much of it empty space contains.

261
00:14:20,640 --> 00:14:22,820
但是当人们清算那个数据
But when they tallied that number

262
00:14:22,940 --> 00:14:26,330
相较于充满粒子波的宇宙
against how much energy empty space ought to have

263
00:14:26,440 --> 00:14:29,230
所应该蕴含的能量
from all the particle waves filling the Universe,

264
00:14:29,340 --> 00:14:31,470
两者之间存在惊人的不匹配
there was a staggering mismatch.

265
00:14:31,580 --> 00:14:34,040
当你统计本该由真空量子效应
When you calculate the amount of energy

266
00:14:34,150 --> 00:14:37,540
所产生能量的多寡时,
that there should be in empty space from quantum effects,

267
00:14:37,650 --> 00:14:41,140
你会得到一个10至120倍大于
you get a number which is 10 to the 120 times larger

268
00:14:41,260 --> 00:14:42,840
加速膨胀的宇宙
than the number that we actually observe

269
00:14:42,960 --> 00:14:45,080
所真实表现出的数值
from the expansion and the acceleration of the Universe.

270
00:14:45,190 --> 00:14:47,480
这是个不正常的数值
And this is an enormous number.

271
00:14:47,600 --> 00:14:50,620
根据他们的统计,
According to their calculations,

272
00:14:50,730 --> 00:14:54,020
空间本身应该有足够能量
there should be enough energy in space itself

273
00:14:54,140 --> 00:14:57,630
足以把整个宇宙蒸干
to boil the Universe away.

274
00:14:57,740 --> 00:14:59,690
但是我们在这好好的
But we are still here.

275
00:14:59,810 --> 00:15:03,200
Neal 以及许多其他的同事觉得他们或许知道
Neal and many of his colleagues think they might know

276
00:15:03,310 --> 00:15:08,070
为什么理论和实际之间的差距如此之大
why such a big mismatch exists between theory and observation.

277
00:15:08,180 --> 00:15:10,870
这或许是因为大多数粒子波
It could be that most particle waves

278
00:15:10,990 --> 00:15:13,780
彼此互相抵消了
are canceling each other out.

279
00:15:13,890 --> 00:15:15,280
波的互相抵消
The cancelation of waves

280
00:15:15,390 --> 00:15:17,310
是个很好理解的现象
is a pretty easy phenomenon to understand.

281
00:15:17,430 --> 00:15:19,380
你只需简单设想假设你有一段波,
You just simply imagine you have one wave,

282
00:15:19,490 --> 00:15:21,680
它有波峰和波谷,
which has peaks and troughs,

283
00:15:21,800 --> 00:15:24,250
然后另一段波，它也有波峰和波谷
and then you have another wave that has peaks and troughs,

284
00:15:24,370 --> 00:15:25,550
当它们相叠加时,
and when those waves combine,

285
00:15:25,670 --> 00:15:27,760
假定波峰或波谷在同一位置 --
if the peaks and troughs are in the same place --

286
00:15:27,870 --> 00:15:30,290
如果两个波峰相遇--它们彼此增强
if I have two peaks in the same place -- they add together.

287
00:15:30,400 --> 00:15:32,560
如果两个波谷相遇
If I have two troughs in the same place,

288
00:15:32,670 --> 00:15:34,130
它们反向叠加增强.
they add together negatively.

289
00:15:34,240 --> 00:15:36,130
但是如果波峰和波谷相遇
But if I have one peak and one trough,

290
00:15:36,240 --> 00:15:38,330
它们抵消了，什么都没给我留下
they cancel out, and I'm left with nothing.

291
00:15:38,450 --> 00:15:39,900
这就叫“干涉”,
And so this interference,

292
00:15:40,010 --> 00:15:42,270
这种波动互相抵消的现象,
this phenomenon of how waves can cancel,

293
00:15:42,380 --> 00:15:43,770
同样会发生在粒子身上
carries over to particles.

294
00:15:43,880 --> 00:15:46,740
Neal 认为有另外一套完整的
Neal thinks there is a whole other set

295
00:15:46,850 --> 00:15:50,650
还未发现的宇宙外粒子,
of as-yet-undetected particles out in the Universe,

296
00:15:50,760 --> 00:15:52,010
它们每一个都制造波动,
each creating waves,

297
00:15:52,130 --> 00:15:55,480
我们所知的粒子波于是乎被其抵消
which cancel out the waves from the particles we know.

298
00:15:55,600 --> 00:15:59,450
这种思想被称为超对称--
It's an idea known as supersymmetry --

299
00:15:59,570 --> 00:16:03,930
每一个粒子都有其镜像同伴
every particle has a mirror-image partner.

300
00:16:04,040 --> 00:16:06,130
如果我的宇宙允许电子存在
The fact that my Universe allows electrons

301
00:16:06,240 --> 00:16:09,430
那就意味着我必须有创造超电子的可能
means that I should have the possibility of creating selectrons.

302
00:16:09,540 --> 00:16:12,370
同样，如果我有夸克，我就得有超夸克
And if I have quarks, I should have squarks.

303
00:16:12,480 --> 00:16:16,240
那Neal的超对称同伴就应该是
And Neal's supersymmetric partner should be...

304
00:16:16,350 --> 00:16:18,940
超Neal.
Sneal.

305
00:16:19,050 --> 00:16:21,810
如果你在纽约，你是一名律师,
If you're in New York, you're either a lawyer,

306
00:16:21,920 --> 00:16:25,250
你搞金融，或者你是演员，我可不会装
you're in finance, or you're an actor, and I can't act.

307
00:16:25,360 --> 00:16:27,450
但是寻找超Neal
But finding Sneal

308
00:16:27,560 --> 00:16:30,550
或者其他超对称粒子波
or any other supersymmetric particle wave

309
00:16:30,670 --> 00:16:33,050
却是个令人沮丧的任务
is a frustrating task.

310
00:16:33,170 --> 00:16:34,490
你可以直接寻找他们
You can look for them directly.

311
00:16:34,600 --> 00:16:35,920
你可以间接寻找他们
You can look for them indirectly.

312
00:16:36,040 --> 00:16:37,990
我费尽心机寻找超对称
I have all sorts of ways to look for supersymmetry.

313
00:16:38,110 --> 00:16:39,460
但时至今日,
But up to this point,

314
00:16:39,570 --> 00:16:42,460
他们都漂亮的躲过了我们的搜索,
it's done an excellent job of hiding from us,

315
00:16:42,580 --> 00:16:44,970
那么究竟是我们即将发现它
so either we're about to find it

316
00:16:45,080 --> 00:16:48,350
还是像我们中很多人想说的那样——它根本就不存在
or I think a lot of us are gonna say it's just not there.

317
00:16:51,150 --> 00:16:56,740
大型强子对撞机到目前为止连超对称粒子的影子都没见到
The LHC has so far seen no sign of supersymmetric particles.

318
00:16:56,860 --> 00:16:59,010
如果它们不存在,
If they do not exist,

319
00:16:59,130 --> 00:17:01,550
科学家们将留下一个莫名其妙的困境--
scientists will be left with a baffling predicament --

320
00:17:01,660 --> 00:17:04,790
怎么解释为何真空能量
explaining why the energy of empty space

321
00:17:04,900 --> 00:17:07,890
没有把宇宙撕成碎片
is not tearing our Universe to shreds.

322
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:09,860
然而另有科学家认为
But other scientists believe

323
00:17:09,970 --> 00:17:14,830
真空的灾难性大爆炸其实是不可避免的
a cataclysmic explosion of nothing is inevitable.

324
00:17:14,940 --> 00:17:18,470
当它可能发生时
And one has worked out

325
00:17:18,580 --> 00:17:20,350
它就会发生
when it might happen.

326
00:17:26,850 --> 00:17:30,250
真空充满宇宙
Empty space fills our cosmos

327
00:17:30,360 --> 00:17:33,680
如同无垠的虚空之海
like a great ocean of nothingness.

328
00:17:33,920 --> 00:17:36,040
但是这所谓的宇宙之水
But the still waters of the Universe

329
00:17:36,160 --> 00:17:38,740
恐怕不会平静太久
may not be tranquil for long.

330
00:17:38,950 --> 00:17:41,540
正如一名科学家所指出的,
As one scientist sees it,

331
00:17:41,660 --> 00:17:44,120
暴风雨正在酝酿
a storm may be brewing.

332
00:17:46,130 --> 00:17:50,120
Max Tegmark是麻省理工学院的一名宇宙学家
Max Tegmark is a cosmologist at M.I.T.

333
00:17:50,390 --> 00:17:54,450
不要被他轻松的魅力所欺骗
Do not let his relaxed charm fool you.

334
00:17:54,560 --> 00:17:57,050
他其实忧虑重重
He is deeply troubled.

335
00:17:57,160 --> 00:17:58,890
他的脑子里全是
What is on his mind

336
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:03,460
有关未来真空的东西
is nothing other than the future of empty space.

337
00:18:03,580 --> 00:18:08,760
空间本身似乎是稳定而永久的,
Space itself seems just imminently stable and permanent,

338
00:18:08,880 --> 00:18:10,700
就如同这些高尔夫球.
just like these golf balls here.

339
00:18:10,810 --> 00:18:14,700
它们已经被打了有些时日了
Been hitting these around for quite a while now,

340
00:18:14,820 --> 00:18:17,000
而且之后看上去它们还是老样子，
and they always look the same afterwards,

341
00:18:17,120 --> 00:18:22,090
但是我怎么就能真正，真正的确定这个材料是稳定的？
but how can I be really, really sure that stuff is stable?

342
00:18:32,130 --> 00:18:36,490
正如高尔夫球最终将归于一团尘埃,
Just like the golf ball changed its state into a cloud of dust,

343
00:18:36,600 --> 00:18:38,960
有朝一日空间本身会否也将
could space itself somehow change its state

344
00:18:39,070 --> 00:18:40,330
沧海变桑田？
into something else?

345
00:18:40,440 --> 00:18:44,730
空间因一个快速衰变转换形态
A rapid decay of space into a different state

346
00:18:44,850 --> 00:18:47,270
或许听起来匪夷所思,
may sound highly unlikely,

347
00:18:47,380 --> 00:18:49,380
但这并非没有先例
but it is not without precedent.

348
00:18:51,980 --> 00:18:54,940
137亿年前,
13.7 billion years ago,

349
00:18:55,060 --> 00:18:57,540
宇宙改变了其基本特性
the Universe shifted its fundamental properties

350
00:18:57,660 --> 00:19:00,110
它的温度也随之下降
and its temperature plummeted.

351
00:19:00,230 --> 00:19:04,220
物理学家称其为“大爆炸”
Physicists call this the Big Bang.

352
00:19:04,330 --> 00:19:06,390
透过最强力的眼睛,
And through Max's eyes,

353
00:19:06,500 --> 00:19:08,370
貌似发现一些异样
there was something fishy about it.

354
00:19:12,110 --> 00:19:13,830
假设我是一条鱼
I pretend I'm a fish.

355
00:19:13,940 --> 00:19:16,400
我一辈子都待在海里,
I've spent my whole life in the ocean,

356
00:19:16,510 --> 00:19:20,270
我觉得水就好像是真空,
and I think of water as just empty space,

357
00:19:20,380 --> 00:19:21,500
那是因为我就知道这些
'cause that's all I know.

358
00:19:21,620 --> 00:19:22,800
直到有一天,
And then one day,

359
00:19:22,920 --> 00:19:25,540
我发现所谓的真空其实是一种物质
I realize that this emptiness is actually a substance.

360
00:19:25,650 --> 00:19:28,410
我是条求知而好奇的鱼,
And I am an interested and curious fish,

361
00:19:28,520 --> 00:19:31,580
所以我指出除了我所处的液态水之外,
so I figure out in addition to the liquid water, which I'm in,

362
00:19:31,690 --> 00:19:35,650
还有固态--冰--以及气态蒸汽
there is this solid phase -- ice -- and there's steam.

363
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:38,890
然后我就开始担心万一有一天, 你懂的,
And then I would start worrying about whether one day, you know,

364
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:40,820
水要是结冰我也得挂了
my water might freeze and I might die.

365
00:19:40,930 --> 00:19:43,360
事实上我们观测我们所处的空间也是同样的情形,
And in exactly the same way we've looked at our space,

366
00:19:43,470 --> 00:19:46,690
我们也意识到空间同样的，也有可能被冻住
realized that it, too, seems to be able to freeze

367
00:19:46,810 --> 00:19:48,010
然后我们就完蛋了
and kill us all.

368
00:19:54,880 --> 00:19:56,540
Max认为大爆炸
Max thinks the Big Bang

369
00:19:56,650 --> 00:20:00,310
并不是宇宙最后一次体验冰冻,
was not the last cosmic freeze our Universe will experience,

370
00:20:00,420 --> 00:20:03,910
他对此的证明基于量子力学中
and his proof lies in the mind-bending science

371
00:20:04,020 --> 00:20:05,810
最令人费解的科学,
of Quantum Mechanics,

372
00:20:05,930 --> 00:20:10,650
任何事物都不是绝对固定，任何事物都不能永恒持续
where nothing is fixed and nothing can last forever.

373
00:20:10,760 --> 00:20:12,750
量子力学会告诉你
Quantum Mechanics tells you that a particle

374
00:20:12,870 --> 00:20:15,260
粒子不能与固定位置
can never be perfectly still

375
00:20:15,370 --> 00:20:17,040
完美匹配
in a known position.

376
00:20:17,970 --> 00:20:19,590
量子力学也同样告诉你
And Quantum Mechanics tells you that

377
00:20:19,710 --> 00:20:21,460
这不仅适用于原子这样的微观粒子,
not just about little things like atoms,

378
00:20:21,580 --> 00:20:23,460
也同样适用于原子构成的宏观物体,
but also about big things that are made of atoms,

379
00:20:23,580 --> 00:20:24,630
比如这些高尔夫球
like this golf ball.

380
00:20:24,740 --> 00:20:29,470
这意味着任何东西都不是完全稳定
Which means nothing is completely stable.

381
00:20:29,580 --> 00:20:32,670
这种物体的量子抖动将永无止境,
This quantum jiggling of things will eventually,

382
00:20:32,790 --> 00:20:35,210
如果我在这站的时间足够长
if I were to stand here long enough,

383
00:20:35,320 --> 00:20:38,880
只因高尔夫球随机往上那么一丁点,
cause the golf ball to just randomly go up a little bit,

384
00:20:38,990 --> 00:20:41,690
然后就直接下降到更低的能量状态
then fall down into a lower energy state.

385
00:20:42,830 --> 00:20:46,250
独自待在球座上，然后经历一个非常微小的变化
Left alone on the tee, there was a very slight chance

386
00:20:46,370 --> 00:20:49,020
这个高尔夫球将隧穿空间
this golf ball will tunnel through space

387
00:20:49,140 --> 00:20:51,560
然后在离地更近的地方实体化,
and materialize closer to the ground,

388
00:20:51,670 --> 00:20:53,660
那里能级更低
where its energy is lower.

389
00:20:53,770 --> 00:20:56,260
当物体隧穿空间时,
When an object tunnels through space,

390
00:20:56,380 --> 00:20:58,770
它几乎能最终处于任何地方
it can end up practically anywhere,

391
00:20:58,880 --> 00:21:02,100
只要它的能量能变低
as long as its energy is lower.

392
00:21:02,220 --> 00:21:04,640
它甚至能隧穿进锡杯中--
It could even tunnel into the tin cup --

393
00:21:04,750 --> 00:21:08,440
不用挥杆就来个一杆进洞
a perfect hole-in-one without even swinging.

394
00:21:08,560 --> 00:21:12,120
但这种现象对宇宙来说可是个坏消息
But this phenomenon could be bad news for the Universe.

395
00:21:13,660 --> 00:21:18,550
我们物理学家已近找到绝好的证据证明
We physicists have found pretty good evidence that space itself

396
00:21:18,670 --> 00:21:20,920
空间本身可以处在几个不同能级--
can be in several different energy states --

397
00:21:21,030 --> 00:21:23,690
低, 中, 高.
lower, medium, higher.

398
00:21:23,800 --> 00:21:25,630
我们也有足够理由相信
And we also have good reason to believe

399
00:21:25,740 --> 00:21:28,260
我们的空间在宇宙早期所处的能级
that our space used to be in a much higher energy state

400
00:21:28,380 --> 00:21:30,700
远高于现在,
in the early Universe,

401
00:21:30,810 --> 00:21:33,200
那时即使粒子能存在的种类
in which even the kinds of particles that could exist

402
00:21:33,310 --> 00:21:34,450
都大不相同
were different.

403
00:21:36,220 --> 00:21:39,670
现在,这个早期宇宙，给我们来了个大爆炸
Now, this early Universe, which gave us our Big Bang,

404
00:21:39,790 --> 00:21:42,310
空间变得不稳定而且快速衰变到
was unstable and very quickly decayed

405
00:21:42,420 --> 00:21:45,580
更低的能级,也就是今天的样子,
into a lower energy state that we inhabit today,

406
00:21:45,690 --> 00:21:48,850
空间平和,美丽且可居住
with this peaceful, very nice, and inhabitable Space

407
00:21:48,960 --> 00:21:52,120
构成我们的那些种粒子赖此而存在
which contains our kinds of particles that we're made of.

408
00:21:52,230 --> 00:21:54,620
但我们同样观测到
But we've also measured

409
00:21:54,730 --> 00:21:57,590
一定还有更低的能级,
that there must be an even lower state,

410
00:21:57,700 --> 00:22:01,400
因为我们所谓的真空并非空无一物
because our empty space, as we call it, isn't empty.

411
00:22:01,510 --> 00:22:03,660
它其实乱成一锅粥,
It has mass, and as such,

412
00:22:03,780 --> 00:22:06,800
那它会否衰变到...
should be able to decay...

413
00:22:06,910 --> 00:22:09,540
比如今更低的能级,
into an even lower energy state,

414
00:22:09,650 --> 00:22:14,240
构成我们的这些粒子将不能存在
where our kinds of particles aren't allowed to exist.

415
00:22:14,350 --> 00:22:16,640
自从我制出那些低能级种类粒子起,
And since I'm made out of that kind of particles,

416
00:22:16,760 --> 00:22:18,410
那就是我霉运的开始
that would be a bit of a bummer for me.

417
00:22:18,530 --> 00:22:22,150
当真空能量大衰变突然发生时,
When this sudden decay in the energy of empty space happens,

418
00:22:22,260 --> 00:22:24,320
一系列急剧破坏性的虚空
a blast of destructive nothingness

419
00:22:24,430 --> 00:22:28,120
将以光速穿行宇宙四处传播
will spread through the Universe at the speed of light.

420
00:22:28,240 --> 00:22:31,340
我们甚至来不及看它一眼
We will have no way to see it coming.

421
00:22:34,070 --> 00:22:35,340
这是不可避免的
It's inevitable.

422
00:22:36,840 --> 00:22:41,770
尽管我们非常不确定，这一切将发生于以后何时
What's very unclear, though, is how long it's gonna last.

423
00:22:41,880 --> 00:22:44,770
你知道，有些物质比其他物质稳定得多
Some things are a lot more stable than others, you know?

424
00:22:44,880 --> 00:22:49,810
一个铀原子能存在亿万斯年，
A uranium atom will last for billions and billions of years,

425
00:22:49,920 --> 00:22:53,280
然而, 据说, 铯137原子
whereas, say, a Cesium-137 atom

426
00:22:53,390 --> 00:22:56,220
从核反应堆中泄露出来后
that leaked out of a nuclear reactor

427
00:22:56,330 --> 00:22:58,850
会崩溃的非常快,
is gonna fall apart much quicker,

428
00:22:58,970 --> 00:23:00,820
这使其危险性更强
making it more dangerous.

429
00:23:00,930 --> 00:23:03,560
我们所处的这个宇宙--
And then this Universe we're in --

430
00:23:03,670 --> 00:23:06,590
你懂的,它都存在140亿年了
you know, we've been here for almost 14 billion years,

431
00:23:06,710 --> 00:23:08,970
但是这并不意味着它会一直这么运转下去
but that doesn't mean it's gonna be around forever.

432
00:23:11,010 --> 00:23:13,030
最保守的估计，
On the conservative side,

433
00:23:13,150 --> 00:23:16,870
Max认为我们有200亿年的时间，
Max thinks we could have 20 billion years left,

434
00:23:16,980 --> 00:23:19,240
但那取决于超对称粒子
but that depends on supersymmetry particles

435
00:23:19,350 --> 00:23:21,540
确实存在--
actually existing --

436
00:23:21,660 --> 00:23:23,940
它就是那个Neal Weiner想要见到
the same particles Neal Weiner is hoping to see

437
00:23:24,060 --> 00:23:29,420
而大型强子对撞机却至今未能发现的粒子
and the LHC has so far failed to find.

438
00:23:29,530 --> 00:23:32,850
没有超对称保持真空稳定，
Without supersymmetry to stabilize empty space,

439
00:23:32,970 --> 00:23:36,360
10亿年之内一切都会完蛋--
it could all end in just one billion years --

440
00:23:36,470 --> 00:23:38,770
这只是宇宙眨一下眼睛而已
the blink of a cosmic eye.

441
00:23:42,470 --> 00:23:44,410
我只能笑笑,因为...
I'm just laughing because...

442
00:23:46,980 --> 00:23:49,640
...在影片《布莱恩的一生》结尾
...at the end of "Life of Brian,"

443
00:23:49,750 --> 00:23:53,440
在这部我最喜欢的大片之一中，他们说，
one of my favorite Monty Python movies, they say,

444
00:23:53,550 --> 00:23:56,780
“我生于无，又归于无
"We come from nothing.We go back to nothing.

445
00:23:56,890 --> 00:23:59,120
我失去了什么？无！”
What have we lost? Nothing!"

446
00:24:02,560 --> 00:24:07,150
无或许是宇宙的起源和归宿,
Nothing could be the beginning and the end of the Universe,

447
00:24:07,270 --> 00:24:11,290
但是还有另一个视角来看待无
but there's another way of looking at nothing.

448
00:24:11,400 --> 00:24:15,530
宇宙或许是一个巨大的气泡
The Universe could be a giant bubble.

449
00:24:15,640 --> 00:24:18,800
所有物质都是...
Everything that is...something

450
00:24:18,910 --> 00:24:20,700
附着其表面的东西
fits on the surface.

451
00:24:20,810 --> 00:24:25,480
而里面的地方只能算是浪费
And the inside is just a waste of space.

452
00:24:28,460 --> 00:24:32,080
当我们观察夜晚闪烁的星光
When we look at the twinkling starlight in the night sky,

453
00:24:32,610 --> 00:24:35,440
很难理解星星与我们之间
it's hard to understand the vast distances

454
00:24:35,550 --> 00:24:38,010
距离如此之远而中间隔着--
that separate us from those stars --

455
00:24:38,120 --> 00:24:42,910
亿万复亿万里的空白
the trillions upon trillions of miles of emptiness.

456
00:24:43,020 --> 00:24:46,150
但这不是古人们的看法
But that's not the way the ancients saw it.

457
00:24:46,260 --> 00:24:49,920
对古人来说，星星只是黑幕上一个光点
To them, the stars were just points of light

458
00:24:50,030 --> 00:24:53,620
而黑幕则笼盖四野
on a black shell that surrounded the Earth.

459
00:24:53,880 --> 00:24:57,030
外太空根本就不存在
Outer space did not exist.

460
00:24:57,150 --> 00:24:58,840
现在一些无畏的思想者
Now some bold thinkers

461
00:24:58,950 --> 00:25:02,540
又重新接受了这个理论--
are embracing this period of this idea again --

462
00:25:02,650 --> 00:25:07,060
这观点已经被抛弃一千多年了
a thousand years after the idea was abandoned.

463
00:25:09,440 --> 00:25:13,200
Gerard't Hooft获得了1999年的诺贝尔物理学奖
Gerard't Hooft won the Nobel Prize in Physics in 1999

464
00:25:13,320 --> 00:25:16,840
因为他建立了--
for his work in establishing the standard model --

465
00:25:16,950 --> 00:25:21,670
现代基本粒子物理学标准模型
the basic foundation of particle physics today.

466
00:25:21,780 --> 00:25:26,040
你可以称他为现代物理的一位王者
You could call him one of the kings of modern physics.

467
00:25:26,150 --> 00:25:30,080
但你也可以叫他光杆大领主
But you could also call him high lord of nothing.

468
00:25:30,190 --> 00:25:33,650
好吧, 几乎 没啥
Well, almost nothing.

469
00:25:33,760 --> 00:25:38,690
因为这块贫瘠的石头是他私人发现的小行星
Because this barren rock is his own private asteroid

470
00:25:38,800 --> 00:25:42,590
它漂浮于距地球一亿英里处
floating 100 million miles from Earth.

471
00:25:42,700 --> 00:25:44,530
国际天文联合会
The international astronomical union

472
00:25:44,640 --> 00:25:49,110
已经决定将该小行星命名为“9491't Hooft”
had decided to name the asteroid "9491't Hooft."

473
00:25:51,040 --> 00:25:54,770
我当然对此事感到高兴和荣耀，
I was, of course, very flattered and honored by the event,

474
00:25:54,880 --> 00:25:56,970
但是有一点让我硌得慌，
but one little thing struck me,

475
00:25:57,080 --> 00:26:01,040
他们把我的姓拼错了
and it was that they changed the spelling of my last name.

476
00:26:01,160 --> 00:26:06,820
它被拼成“Thooft”，开头字母是“T”
It now became "Thooft," with a capital "T"

477
00:26:06,930 --> 00:26:09,320
而 "hooft"只是被放在右边，
and then "hooft" just spelled right after it,

478
00:26:09,430 --> 00:26:11,030
左边没撇号
without apostrophe.

479
00:26:13,200 --> 00:26:16,160
Gerard计划报复--
Gerard planned revenge --

480
00:26:16,270 --> 00:26:18,160
诗意盎然的报复
a poetic revenge.

481
00:26:18,270 --> 00:26:23,400
我决定为这颗小行星定一部宪法,
I decided that the asteroid would require a constitution,

482
00:26:23,510 --> 00:26:27,600
宪法的其中一项重要条款就是
and one of the first items in the constitution

483
00:26:27,720 --> 00:26:31,840
未来所有在这颗小行星上的定居者
is that all future inhabitants of this asteroid

484
00:26:31,950 --> 00:26:35,510
都必须和撇号说拜拜
would have to live without apostrophes.

485
00:26:35,620 --> 00:26:39,750
无论谁进入该小行星的区域
Anyone entering the territorial zone of the asteroid

486
00:26:39,860 --> 00:26:41,820
比如说带了个手提电脑,
with a laptop, for instance,

487
00:26:41,930 --> 00:26:45,120
这电脑还配了个刻上撇号的钥匙,
that carries a key with an apostrophe in it,

488
00:26:45,230 --> 00:26:48,020
那么这个手提电脑钥匙就必须离开
that key of the laptop would have to be removed.

489
00:26:48,140 --> 00:26:51,130
作为小行星的山大王,
As King of his asteroid,

490
00:26:51,240 --> 00:26:54,700
Gerard有禁止撇号的自由
Gerard is free to ban apostrophes.

491
00:26:54,810 --> 00:26:59,300
但是作为诺贝尔奖获得者，他得承认它们（撇号）依然存在
But as a Nobel laureate, he knows they still exist.

492
00:26:59,410 --> 00:27:03,810
事实上, Gerard认为万事万物都
In fact, Gerard believes that anything that is something

493
00:27:03,920 --> 00:27:07,580
不能在宇宙中被彻底抹杀
can never truly be removed from the Universe.

494
00:27:07,690 --> 00:27:12,550
这一原则被称为信息守恒
It's a principle called the conservation of information.

495
00:27:12,660 --> 00:27:13,750
你或许认为
You might think

496
00:27:13,860 --> 00:27:15,550
人们装进文档的信息
that the information people put in documents

497
00:27:15,660 --> 00:27:18,190
总有一天会像这样完全丢失，
is completely lost once it's like this,

498
00:27:18,300 --> 00:27:20,220
但其实那不是真的
but actually that's not true.

499
00:27:20,330 --> 00:27:24,190
我能把它重新翻出来并把所有碎片拼成一体
I could dig it up and I can try to put all the pieces together.

500
00:27:24,310 --> 00:27:26,360
信息依然保存在那里
The information is still in it.

501
00:27:26,470 --> 00:27:31,430
像Gerard这样的物理学家们认为宇宙中的一切
Physicists like Gerard believe anything in the Universe

502
00:27:31,550 --> 00:27:34,070
都能被一系列字符所描述,
can be described by a series of bits,

503
00:27:34,180 --> 00:27:36,840
也就是一串1或0喽，
or ones and zeros,

504
00:27:36,950 --> 00:27:41,910
无论纸、行星还是恒星，都成立
whether it is a piece of paper, a planet, or a star.

505
00:27:42,020 --> 00:27:43,650
但在宇宙的某处
But there is one place in the cosmos

506
00:27:43,760 --> 00:27:46,280
该理论好像失效了--
where this theory seems to fall apart --

507
00:27:46,390 --> 00:27:47,750
黑洞--
black holes --

508
00:27:47,860 --> 00:27:53,860
贪婪的将所有靠近它的物体清零
rapacious voids that pull in everything that gets too close.

509
00:27:54,040 --> 00:27:56,160
黑洞可比
The black hole is much better

510
00:27:56,270 --> 00:27:58,130
这些粉碎机厉害的多
than any of these shredders here.

511
00:27:58,240 --> 00:27:59,830
在黑洞中，
In a black hole,

512
00:27:59,940 --> 00:28:02,830
信息不仅仅被粉碎，
the information is not only shredded,

513
00:28:02,940 --> 00:28:04,830
它彻底 消失了
it completely disappears.

514
00:28:04,950 --> 00:28:07,340
在20世纪70年代，
In the 1970s,

515
00:28:07,450 --> 00:28:09,970
传奇宇宙学家 史蒂芬 霍金
legendary cosmologist Stephen Hawking

516
00:28:10,080 --> 00:28:13,140
讨论了黑洞自可见宇宙
argued that black holes entirely remove objects

517
00:28:13,250 --> 00:28:14,880
彻底清除物体的问题，
from our visible Universe,

518
00:28:14,990 --> 00:28:19,380
被吞噬的信息似乎永久丢失了
and the information they swallow is gone forever.

519
00:28:19,490 --> 00:28:22,320
这一概念引起了Gerard的强烈质疑
It was a notion that deeply troubled Gerard.

520
00:28:22,430 --> 00:28:23,720
我曾说道，
And I said,

521
00:28:23,830 --> 00:28:28,060
“这不符合我们对物理学的看法”
"that doesn't fit with the view we have about physics."

522
00:28:28,170 --> 00:28:31,290
据我们所知有关原子内外的观点，
From the point of view of what we know about the atoms

523
00:28:31,410 --> 00:28:34,560
信息并不会消失
and what's inside an atom, information doesn't go away.

524
00:28:34,680 --> 00:28:35,830
它不能消失
It can't.

525
00:28:35,940 --> 00:28:38,800
那会违反我们所知的物理定律
It would be against the laws of physics that we know.

526
00:28:38,910 --> 00:28:41,740
霍金则固执己见，
Hawking stood his ground,

527
00:28:41,850 --> 00:28:44,140
两者间的辩论持续数年，
and the two debated for years,

528
00:28:44,250 --> 00:28:48,680
直到一个天才的洞察扭转局面
until a brilliant insight turned the tide.

529
00:28:48,790 --> 00:28:52,410
Gerard意识到如果小行星9491 Thooft
Gerard realized that if 9491 Thooft

530
00:28:52,530 --> 00:28:54,150
掉进了黑洞，
ever fell into a black hole,

531
00:28:54,260 --> 00:28:57,490
它不会消失得无法追溯
it would not disappear without a trace.

532
00:28:57,600 --> 00:29:00,920
它会轻微的改变黑洞
It would ever so slightly change the black hole.

533
00:29:01,040 --> 00:29:04,430
黑洞会变为另一个状态，
The black hole would go into a different state,

534
00:29:04,540 --> 00:29:07,530
于是乎此黑洞非彼黑洞
so the black hole would not be the same black hole

535
00:29:07,640 --> 00:29:09,900
再不是吃我小行星的那个
as it was before it ate my asteroid.

536
00:29:10,010 --> 00:29:12,300
它成了另一个不同的黑洞
It would be a different black hole.

537
00:29:12,410 --> 00:29:17,970
黑洞拜小行星所赐，它长大了，
When a black hole feeds on its prey, it grows,

538
00:29:18,090 --> 00:29:21,710
所以它的表面积会有微小增加
and so its surface area gets slightly larger.

539
00:29:21,820 --> 00:29:24,410
当Gerard统计究竟有多少
And when Gerard calculated exactly how much

540
00:29:24,530 --> 00:29:27,650
净信息量反映在增加的表面积上，
extra information could fit onto this larger surface,

541
00:29:27,760 --> 00:29:30,320
他发现刚好足够把
he discovered it was just enough to fit

542
00:29:30,430 --> 00:29:34,670
黑洞大餐中的所有信息都储存进去
all the information contained in the black hole's dinner.

543
00:29:36,270 --> 00:29:39,260
你扔进黑洞的所有信息
The amount of information you could put in a black hole

544
00:29:39,370 --> 00:29:41,130
都完好无损
is very precisely fine

545
00:29:41,240 --> 00:29:44,570
相应的它们反映于黑洞表面
and is proportional to its surface area.

546
00:29:44,680 --> 00:29:47,870
它不是在表面下
It's not what's inside the surface.

547
00:29:47,980 --> 00:29:50,070
里面无法被统计
It simply doesn't count.

548
00:29:50,180 --> 00:29:53,740
它是表面上的内容,不仅仅是量
It's the surface area that counts, not the volume.

549
00:29:53,850 --> 00:29:57,680
这意味着Gerard那个必死无疑的小行星
This means that the entire information content

550
00:29:57,790 --> 00:30:00,050
以及其它被黑洞吞噬的物质
of Gerard's doomed asteroid

551
00:30:00,160 --> 00:30:02,920
所有信息的内容
and everything else devoured by the black hole

552
00:30:03,030 --> 00:30:06,290
都被印在了黑洞表面上
is imprinted across its surface area.

553
00:30:06,400 --> 00:30:09,490
Gerard发现这一原则
And Gerard discovered that this principle

554
00:30:09,600 --> 00:30:12,330
不单可用于黑洞
applies to more than just black holes.

555
00:30:12,440 --> 00:30:14,900
事实上，信息会储存在
In fact, the information contained

556
00:30:15,010 --> 00:30:18,100
任何三维卷曲之上
inside any three-dimensional volume of space

557
00:30:18,210 --> 00:30:23,040
而空间则附着于卷曲表面
must fit onto that volume's surface area.

558
00:30:23,150 --> 00:30:27,610
你看这个盒子被网格覆盖，
You see that the box is covered by a grid,

559
00:30:27,720 --> 00:30:30,810
当你观测盒子的各种量时
and the amount of information no longer can be counted

560
00:30:30,930 --> 00:30:33,280
其中的信息量将无法计算，
while looking at the volume of the box,

561
00:30:33,390 --> 00:30:35,820
但是通过观察盒子的表面
but by looking at the surface of the box.

562
00:30:35,930 --> 00:30:40,860
通过网格的各个方面，能得到一系列信息
On every side of this grid, there's one bit of information.

563
00:30:40,970 --> 00:30:45,730
把整个宇宙的各方面想象成一个盒子
Think of a box the size of the entire Universe.

564
00:30:45,840 --> 00:30:48,630
所有的信息都整洁的储存在
All of the information\ contained inside

565
00:30:48,740 --> 00:30:51,430
附着其表面的网格上
fits neatly on a grid on the surface.

566
00:30:51,550 --> 00:30:55,670
古往今来万事万物的所有信息
The total information content of everything that ever was

567
00:30:55,780 --> 00:30:57,110
都可在那里被测算
can be counted there.

568
00:30:57,220 --> 00:31:00,410
相比之下信息存在盒子里
Compared with how much space for information

569
00:31:00,520 --> 00:31:02,810
所需要的空间大小，
exists inside the box,

570
00:31:02,920 --> 00:31:05,090
几乎为零
it is practically nothing at all.

571
00:31:08,560 --> 00:31:11,320
理论上, 是的, 你可以--
In principle, yes, you can --

572
00:31:11,430 --> 00:31:13,520
有这种可能
it should be possible

573
00:31:13,630 --> 00:31:16,120
描述宇宙所发生的一切
to describe everything happening in the Universe

574
00:31:16,240 --> 00:31:20,970
仅通过凝聚那个环绕宇宙的表面
by concentrating on a surface surrounding it.

575
00:31:22,380 --> 00:31:26,530
如果他是正确的--（其实大多数物理学家都支持他）
If he is correct -- and most physicists now think he is --

576
00:31:26,650 --> 00:31:30,570
宇宙几乎是浪费空间
the Universe is mostly a waste of space.

577
00:31:30,680 --> 00:31:32,840
因为哪里没有信息，
Because where there is no information,

578
00:31:32,950 --> 00:31:35,520
哪里就真的...啥都没有
there is really...nothing.

579
00:31:36,860 --> 00:31:38,910
但是这位女士令有关无的理论
But this woman has taken the concept of nothing

580
00:31:39,030 --> 00:31:40,920
更上一层楼
one step further.

581
00:31:41,030 --> 00:31:46,350
事实上，她或许发现了我们身边的另一个宇宙，
In fact, she may have found another Universe inside our own,

582
00:31:46,470 --> 00:31:49,470
它几乎空无一物
made of absolutely nothing.

583
00:31:55,090 --> 00:31:59,780
如果我闭上双眼而四周万籁俱寂，
If I close my eyes and nothing makes a sound,

584
00:31:59,890 --> 00:32:03,680
我怎么才能确定世界就在哪里？
how can I be sure the world is really there?

585
00:32:03,900 --> 00:32:10,260
或者...如果你看不到也听不到我，怎样--
Or...if you can't see or hear me, how --

586
00:32:10,370 --> 00:32:13,440
你怎样才能知道我的存在？
how do you know I really exist?

587
00:32:13,550 --> 00:32:16,840
有无之间的差别
The difference between something and nothing

588
00:32:16,950 --> 00:32:19,990
可能只是知觉的问题
could be a matter of perception.

589
00:32:29,600 --> 00:32:31,850
Katie Freese是一名天体物理学家
Katie Freese is an astrophysicist

590
00:32:31,970 --> 00:32:33,730
她富有竞争精神
with a competitive spirit.

591
00:32:35,100 --> 00:32:38,690
我想这源于我的童年时代，
I think this stems from my childhood,

592
00:32:38,810 --> 00:32:43,030
因为我住在两个街区的拐角处,
because we lived on the corner of two blocks,

593
00:32:43,150 --> 00:32:45,600
所有的孩子都从我家门前过
and all the kids came over to my house

594
00:32:45,710 --> 00:32:49,580
去打棒球和篮球或者其它什么，
to play baseball and basketball or whatever,

595
00:32:49,700 --> 00:32:50,920
都是男孩子在玩，
except it was all boys,

596
00:32:51,030 --> 00:32:53,120
所以我经常和男孩一起玩
so I was always playing with the boys.

597
00:32:53,310 --> 00:32:55,570
作为一名物理学家，我依然不改本色
And as a physicist, I'm still doing that.

598
00:32:55,680 --> 00:32:57,930
所以我认为正是那里培养了我的
And  so I think that's where I developed

599
00:32:58,050 --> 00:33:02,240
竞争意识我觉得这挺有趣
this sense of competition and thinking that it's fun.

600
00:33:02,350 --> 00:33:04,670
当她不在球场时，
When she's not on the courts,

601
00:33:04,790 --> 00:33:07,010
Katie就专注于她的心事
Katie peers into the heart of matter

602
00:33:07,120 --> 00:33:11,330
她试图理解是什么令世界充实
and tries to understand what makes it solid.

603
00:33:13,400 --> 00:33:17,190
当我们审视周围的世界，它似乎是实心的
When we look at the world around us, it seems to be really solid.

604
00:33:17,300 --> 00:33:20,120
它看似实心, 它感觉像是实心，但其实它不是
It looks solid, it feels solid, but it's not.

605
00:33:20,240 --> 00:33:23,690
这个网球感觉上是实心的，
This tennis ball feels solid,

606
00:33:23,810 --> 00:33:25,810
但当我们切开它...
but when I cut it open...

607
00:33:28,110 --> 00:33:29,670
...里面是空的--
...it's empty --

608
00:33:29,780 --> 00:33:32,150
就像大多数的物质一样
just like most of matter.

609
00:33:34,980 --> 00:33:37,510
那么,想想我指尖上的
So, if we think about one grain of the sugar

610
00:33:37,620 --> 00:33:39,110
一粒糖，
that's on my fingertip,

611
00:33:39,220 --> 00:33:42,050
假设它相当于原子核，
and if that were equivalent to the nucleus,

612
00:33:42,160 --> 00:33:44,550
那么它将与整个网球场大的地方
then it would take this entire big tennis court

613
00:33:44,660 --> 00:33:45,680
组成原子，
to make up the atom,

614
00:33:45,800 --> 00:33:47,380
相对于糖粒，
and in between the sugar,

615
00:33:47,500 --> 00:33:50,150
原子核所占的只是一丁点
the single grain that makes the nucleus

616
00:33:50,270 --> 00:33:51,890
而整个网球场大的地方，
and this entire tennis court,

617
00:33:52,000 --> 00:33:53,520
实际上什么都没有
there's absolutely nothing.

618
00:33:53,640 --> 00:33:55,670
它是空的
It's empty.

619
00:33:57,710 --> 00:34:01,300
周围的实心世界仅仅是一个幻觉
The solid world around us is merely an illusion.

620
00:34:01,410 --> 00:34:03,200
令物体感觉像实心的东西
What makes things feel solid

621
00:34:03,310 --> 00:34:06,070
莫过于作用于原子最外层
is nothing more than the repulsion of electrons

622
00:34:06,180 --> 00:34:09,240
的电斥力
that exist on the outer shells of atoms.

623
00:34:09,350 --> 00:34:12,540
如果你感受不到这种力，
And if you did not feel this force,

624
00:34:12,660 --> 00:34:17,210
你将能在实心物体处穿墙而过
you could pass right through solid matter.

625
00:34:17,330 --> 00:34:18,950
在过去的二十年里，
In the past two decades,

626
00:34:19,060 --> 00:34:21,420
天文学家发现光线
astronomers have discovered light

627
00:34:21,530 --> 00:34:24,450
弯曲于每一个星系周围
bending around gargantuan invisible masses

628
00:34:24,570 --> 00:34:27,060
看不见的巨大物质团
surrounding every galaxy.

629
00:34:27,170 --> 00:34:30,890
他们认为这些物质团由暗物质构成
They believe these masses are made of dark matter.

630
00:34:31,010 --> 00:34:32,330
之所以说它“暗”
They call it dark

631
00:34:32,440 --> 00:34:36,130
那是因为我们不能看到它，感受它，或者触摸它
because we cannot see it, feel it, or touch it.

632
00:34:36,250 --> 00:34:38,740
它从我们的实心世界穿过
It passes right through our solid world

633
00:34:38,850 --> 00:34:41,710
就好像什么都没发生一样
as if it was not there at all.

634
00:34:41,820 --> 00:34:43,270
迄今为止有关暗物质，
As far as dark matter goes,

635
00:34:43,390 --> 00:34:45,980
我们知道它从不发生电磁作用
we know that it does not have electric charge.

636
00:34:46,090 --> 00:34:47,540
我们得知道
We would know.

637
00:34:47,660 --> 00:34:50,080
我的意思是，这些东西可能会轰击你，你得知道
I mean, these things would be bombarding you, and you'd know.

638
00:34:50,190 --> 00:34:52,350
每秒可能有数十亿计的暗物质粒子
There are probably billions of dark-matter particles

639
00:34:52,460 --> 00:34:54,150
穿过我们的身体
passing through our bodies every second.

640
00:34:54,260 --> 00:34:56,750
Katie认为暗物质
Katie believes that dark matter

641
00:34:56,870 --> 00:35:00,190
是由与普通物质一样重的粒子构成，
is made up of particles just as heavy as regular matter,

642
00:35:00,300 --> 00:35:02,160
但唯一与它们作用的力
but they are only affected

643
00:35:02,270 --> 00:35:05,360
是科学家所称的“弱力”--
by what scientists call the weak force --

644
00:35:05,470 --> 00:35:09,300
该力如此微弱，我们大部分精密仪器
a force so puny, its effect is barely detectable

645
00:35:09,410 --> 00:35:12,470
都检测不到它的效应
by our most sophisticated equipment.

646
00:35:12,580 --> 00:35:14,700
在我的右手，握有一个网球拍，
In my right hand, I have a tennis racket,

647
00:35:14,820 --> 00:35:17,140
在我的左手，我有一杯糖，
and in my left hand, I have a glass of sugar,

648
00:35:17,250 --> 00:35:19,080
我们将用这两样道具
and we're gonna use these as props

649
00:35:19,190 --> 00:35:22,060
来解释弱相互作用
to explain weak interactions.

650
00:35:23,160 --> 00:35:25,120
这些弦代表普通物质
The strings are representing regular matter

651
00:35:25,230 --> 00:35:26,920
它们间有很大空隙，
with a lot of space in between them,

652
00:35:27,030 --> 00:35:29,020
所以当糖粒穿过时,
so when the grains of sugar go through,

653
00:35:29,130 --> 00:35:30,890
它们之中的大多数只是直穿而过
most of them just pass right on by

654
00:35:31,000 --> 00:35:33,990
而不发生任何作用
without having any interaction whatsoever.

655
00:35:34,100 --> 00:35:37,090
Katie 认为一天之内,
Katie believes that in one day,

656
00:35:37,210 --> 00:35:39,460
在穿过你身体的几十亿
of the few billion particles of dark matter

657
00:35:39,580 --> 00:35:40,960
暗物质粒子中，
that pass through your body,

658
00:35:41,080 --> 00:35:42,570
只有两三个
only two or three of them

659
00:35:42,680 --> 00:35:45,470
能与你身体内的原子发生作用
will ever interact with the atoms inside you.

660
00:35:45,580 --> 00:35:47,670
而且当他们作用时，
And when they do,

661
00:35:47,780 --> 00:35:50,840
也只是通过弱力作用
it is only through the weak force.

662
00:35:50,950 --> 00:35:53,180
全世界的高灵敏度实验
Highly sensitive experiments around the world

663
00:35:53,290 --> 00:35:55,750
已经试图探测这种罕见的相互作用
have been trying to detect these rare interactions

664
00:35:55,860 --> 00:35:57,280
超过10年了，
for over a decade,

665
00:35:57,390 --> 00:36:00,850
但不同的实验却互相矛盾
but the experiments do not agree with one another.

666
00:36:00,960 --> 00:36:05,360
其中一个实验花费十年时间观测信号，
One of the experiments has been seeing a signal for 10 years,

667
00:36:05,470 --> 00:36:08,860
得出的统计结果也非常显著
and it's a statistically very significant result.

668
00:36:08,970 --> 00:36:11,360
但问题是另一些实验
But the problem is that some of the other experiments

669
00:36:11,470 --> 00:36:13,760
则不支持理论，因为他们什么也没看到
are in disagreement because they're not seeing anything.

670
00:36:13,880 --> 00:36:16,370
问题就是，这究竟是怎么回事？
The question is, what's going on?

671
00:36:16,480 --> 00:36:18,330
如同科学竞赛一般
As a scientist competing

672
00:36:18,450 --> 00:36:21,170
身处最大的物理理论游戏之一，
in one of the biggest theoretical games in physics,

673
00:36:21,280 --> 00:36:25,440
Katie开始担心一个初露端倪的可能性
Katie is beginning to worry about an emerging possibility.

674
00:36:25,550 --> 00:36:29,580
暗物质恐怕连弱力都感受不到
Dark matter may not even feel the weak force.

675
00:36:29,690 --> 00:36:31,180
多么可怕的想法
What a horrible thought.

676
00:36:31,290 --> 00:36:34,320
没人说暗物质必须得弱相互作用，
Nobody said the dark matter had to weakly interact,

677
00:36:34,430 --> 00:36:37,350
所以之后我们就有了个问题
so then we really have a problem.

678
00:36:37,470 --> 00:36:39,890
我不知道怎样才能探测到它
Then I don't know how we're ever gonna detect it.

679
00:36:40,000 --> 00:36:42,660
又怎样才能发现它？
How can we discover it?

680
00:36:42,770 --> 00:36:44,890
这可真令人丧气
That would be really discouraging.

681
00:36:45,010 --> 00:36:47,070
所以我希望事实并非如此
So let's hope not.

682
00:36:49,380 --> 00:36:51,530
如果这确实是事实，
If this is the case,

683
00:36:51,650 --> 00:36:55,070
我们的宇宙将被分成两个世界--
our Universe is divided into two worlds --

684
00:36:55,180 --> 00:36:59,320
一个是物质的，另一个是暗物质的
one of matter and one of dark matter.

685
00:37:07,430 --> 00:37:11,100
它们互为对方的真空
And they will always be nothing to each other.

686
00:37:16,600 --> 00:37:20,040
好像球拍没网格的网球比赛
Like a tennis game where the rackets have no strings.

687
00:37:29,650 --> 00:37:33,580
对宇宙质量贡献最大的
The most important contribution to the mass in the Universe

688
00:37:33,690 --> 00:37:36,890
恐怕还真主要是真空
could really basically be nothingness.

689
00:37:38,690 --> 00:37:41,320
所以真空统治一切
So nothingness would rule.

690
00:37:41,430 --> 00:37:44,590
但是有没有这样的地方
But is there or was there

691
00:37:44,700 --> 00:37:48,160
那里绝对啥也没有？
ever such a thing as absolute nothing?

692
00:37:48,270 --> 00:37:52,460
没能量，没物质，没时空
No energy, no matter, no time or space.

693
00:37:52,580 --> 00:37:54,030
对这个问题的答案
The answer to this question

694
00:37:54,140 --> 00:37:58,940
或许会揭示宇宙的终极起源，
might reveal the ultimate origin of our cosmos,

695
00:37:59,050 --> 00:38:03,350
这个科学先锋认为他已经找到了
and this scientific pioneer thinks he has found it.

696
00:38:04,610 --> 00:38:06,600
仅在十年前，
Only a decade ago,

697
00:38:07,030 --> 00:38:12,390
天文学家们证实了很大程度上似乎完全不可能的事
astronomers confirmed what to many seemed utterly impossible.

698
00:38:12,610 --> 00:38:16,030
追溯到137亿年前,
Go back 13.7 billion years,

699
00:38:16,150 --> 00:38:18,870
那里只有黑暗
and there was only darkness.

700
00:38:19,100 --> 00:38:25,100
然后我们的宇宙在爆炸中诞生
Then our Universe exploded into existence.

701
00:38:25,240 --> 00:38:30,480
万物是怎么生于无的？
How could everything come from nothing?

702
00:38:32,380 --> 00:38:35,870
Gabriele Veneziano是弦理论之父，
Gabriele Veneziano is the father of String Theory,

703
00:38:35,980 --> 00:38:39,180
弦理论成了现代物理最重要的
which has become one of the most important scientific ideas

704
00:38:39,290 --> 00:38:40,980
的科学思想之一
in modern physics.

705
00:38:41,090 --> 00:38:45,680
但是他最后的大想法挑战着他的思想主流
But his latest big idea challenges the mainstream.

706
00:38:45,790 --> 00:38:47,620
他认为大爆炸
He believes the Big Bang

707
00:38:47,730 --> 00:38:51,450
并不是万物的源泉
could not have been the beginning of everything.

708
00:38:51,570 --> 00:38:54,160
宇宙生于无的结论--
The conclusion that there was nothing --

709
00:38:54,270 --> 00:38:56,690
我认为这结论下得太快，
I think it was too fast a conclusion,

710
00:38:56,810 --> 00:38:59,560
所以我不愿重复这一错误
so I don't want to repeat the same mistake.

711
00:38:59,680 --> 00:39:03,030
Gabriele认为在大爆炸之前
Gabriele believes that there was something

712
00:39:03,150 --> 00:39:05,030
有东西
before the Big Bang.

713
00:39:05,150 --> 00:39:07,740
但是，正如拂晓时的城市，
But, like a city at daybreak,

714
00:39:07,850 --> 00:39:11,470
前宇宙的大部分很快睡了
most of this pre-Universe was fast asleep.

715
00:39:11,590 --> 00:39:15,610
一些东西在空间传播，
There were things propagating in space,

716
00:39:15,720 --> 00:39:18,780
像是波，粒子，
like waves, particles,

717
00:39:18,890 --> 00:39:21,650
但能量却很稀薄，
but the energy was very diluted,

718
00:39:21,760 --> 00:39:23,050
此外，
and furthermore,

719
00:39:23,170 --> 00:39:27,370
这些波或粒子之间的作用非常非常弱
this wave or this particle interacted very, very weakly.

720
00:39:28,970 --> 00:39:33,630
这就好比大街上只有几个人散步
That would be like having very few people walking in the street

721
00:39:33,740 --> 00:39:37,400
与此同时，他们之间没影响
and, furthermore, not interacting with each other.

722
00:39:37,510 --> 00:39:39,700
他们彼此不说话
They may not talk to each other.

723
00:39:39,820 --> 00:39:43,080
他们也感受不到对方
They may not feel each other.

724
00:39:44,820 --> 00:39:46,610
Gabriele认为
Gabriele believes

725
00:39:46,720 --> 00:39:50,580
今天我们所知的自然基本力
that the same fundamental forces of nature we know today

726
00:39:50,690 --> 00:39:52,580
在前宇宙同样存在，
existed in the pre-Universe,

727
00:39:52,690 --> 00:39:55,020
但是它们的力度却小得多
but their strengths were much lower.

728
00:39:55,130 --> 00:39:57,350
所有这些力的力度
The strength of all these forces

729
00:39:57,470 --> 00:40:02,660
都根据我们所称的“伸缩场”
was given in terms of what we call a dilaton field.

730
00:40:02,770 --> 00:40:06,800
这种伸缩场充满整个前宇宙
This dilaton field filled the entire pre-Universe

731
00:40:06,910 --> 00:40:10,200
它控制着所有力的力度
and controlled the strength of all the forces.

732
00:40:10,310 --> 00:40:13,070
正如大家逐渐被吵醒，
As it gradually dialed them all up,

733
00:40:13,180 --> 00:40:15,500
一些事情开始发生
things started to happen.

734
00:40:15,620 --> 00:40:19,180
随时间流逝，行人的密度也开始增加
As time goes on, the density of people is increasing.

735
00:40:19,290 --> 00:40:20,480
最后，
As a result,

736
00:40:20,590 --> 00:40:24,450
联系性变得越来越强
the interactions are getting stronger and stronger.

737
00:40:24,560 --> 00:40:28,750
所以，你看到人们走在一起，一起交谈，
So, you see people getting together, talking together,

738
00:40:28,860 --> 00:40:33,090
也扎堆在一起
making clusters of people together.

739
00:40:33,200 --> 00:40:36,190
压力与日俱增
The ever-growing pressure increases

740
00:40:36,310 --> 00:40:41,100
联系性也增强，直到...
and the interactions intensify until...

741
00:40:41,210 --> 00:40:42,440
一切爆发出来
Things blow up.

742
00:40:49,450 --> 00:40:50,770
对Gabriele来说，
For Gabriele,

743
00:40:50,890 --> 00:40:53,340
大爆炸不是一次突然开始，
the Big Bang was not a sudden beginning,

744
00:40:53,460 --> 00:40:55,010
更像是一个引爆点
but rather a tipping point.

745
00:40:55,120 --> 00:40:57,080
如果他是对的，
If he is right,

746
00:40:57,190 --> 00:41:01,050
他将调和最令人费解的矛盾--
he will have dispensed its most puzzling paradox --

747
00:41:01,160 --> 00:41:04,490
无中生有
getting something from nothing.

748
00:41:04,600 --> 00:41:07,790
证明宇宙从不是一无所有
Proving there was never nothing in the Universe

749
00:41:07,900 --> 00:41:10,530
或许并不如你想象的那般困难
may not be as difficult as you think.

750
00:41:10,640 --> 00:41:14,000
因为如果空间和物质一直存在，
Because if space and matter have always existed,

751
00:41:14,110 --> 00:41:17,030
大爆炸将会发出巨大的引力波
the Big Bang should have sent colossal gravitational waves

752
00:41:17,150 --> 00:41:18,930
波纹穿过一切，
rippling through them,

753
00:41:19,050 --> 00:41:21,440
而那些波浪的余威
and the aftershock of those waves

754
00:41:21,550 --> 00:41:25,150
至今依旧可以探测
may still be detectable today.

755
00:41:28,420 --> 00:41:30,910
如果我们能发现引力波，
If we could see gravitational waves,

756
00:41:31,030 --> 00:41:35,120
我们就能追溯更早,更早之前
we could go back much, much earlier,

757
00:41:35,230 --> 00:41:38,120
理论上非常,非常接近大爆炸
ideally very, very close with the Big Bang.

758
00:41:38,230 --> 00:41:41,320
抑或如果有什么早于大爆炸，
Or if there was something before the Big Bang,

759
00:41:41,440 --> 00:41:44,360
我们甚至能观测
we can even go back to looking at the Universe

760
00:41:44,470 --> 00:41:45,960
大爆炸前的宇宙
before the Big Bang.

761
00:41:46,070 --> 00:41:50,730
如果前宇宙存在时发出的引力波至今还有剩余，
If gravitational waves left over from the pre-Universe exist,

762
00:41:50,850 --> 00:41:52,640
它们应该会非常轻微的
they should be ever so slightly

763
00:41:52,750 --> 00:41:56,470
拉伸和压扁我们周围的空间
stretching and squashing the spaces around us.

764
00:41:56,590 --> 00:41:58,240
全球的工程师们
Engineers from around the world

765
00:41:58,350 --> 00:42:01,040
正提交一种新飞船的设计方案
are submitting designs for a new spacecraft

766
00:42:01,160 --> 00:42:03,980
它敏感得足以探测这种扭曲
sensitive enough to detect these distortions.

767
00:42:04,090 --> 00:42:08,720
重要的是我们有实验途径
The important thing is that there are experimental ways

768
00:42:08,830 --> 00:42:11,090
来描述这些东西
to talk about these things.

769
00:42:11,200 --> 00:42:14,190
我的意思是，它们不纯是科幻小说
I mean, they're not just pure science fiction.

770
00:42:14,300 --> 00:42:17,060
我的意思是,你能检验这个模型
I mean, you can put this model to a test.

771
00:42:17,170 --> 00:42:19,360
Gabriele的任务
Gabriele's mission

772
00:42:19,470 --> 00:42:23,670
旨在证明空无从未存在也不会存在
to prove that nothing does not exist and never did

773
00:42:23,780 --> 00:42:26,580
他或许就在成功的边缘
may be on the verge of success.

774
00:42:28,180 --> 00:42:30,240
古希腊人认为绝对的无
The ancient Greeks thought of nothing

775
00:42:30,350 --> 00:42:33,640
在逻辑上是不可能的
as a logical impossibility.

776
00:42:33,760 --> 00:42:38,110
你在思考无的时候，它已经成了有
The moment you think about nothing, it becomes something.

777
00:42:38,230 --> 00:42:40,920
现代科学家们已经花费数百年时间
Modern scientists have spent centuries

778
00:42:41,030 --> 00:42:43,350
思考无的问题，
thinking about nothing,

779
00:42:43,470 --> 00:42:47,560
他们的研究结果表明古希腊人是对的
and what they've learned proved the greeks were right.

780
00:42:47,670 --> 00:42:49,020
那里或许有足够的能量
There may be enough energy

781
00:42:49,140 --> 00:42:52,160
泛起的涟漪将穿过真空摧毁我们，
rippling through nothingness to destroy us,

782
00:42:52,270 --> 00:42:55,230
整个宇宙或许都由其构成，
entire Universes may be made of it,

783
00:42:55,340 --> 00:43:00,550
而且我们能十分确定那并不空
And it is most definitely not nothing.

